          "text": "{\"answer_text\":\"No. Different targets do not automatically make two evidence records independent confirmations. The records could share a dataset, experimental methods, authors, or an underlying source, and they may support different claims. Independence requires checking their provenance and what each record actually establishes. No records were supplied, so this cannot be assessed here. This is an unverified development control, not clinical advice.\",\"claims\":[],\"unanswered\":[\"What are the two records, their sources, and their underlying data and methods?\",\"Do the records support the same specific claim?\"]}"
